{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786606250108,"sessionID":"ses_005f8753cffeGq3BHa2N564TRT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_6tWsMqPIJsrmWxx4k3kM8676","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/iterations/iteration-001-retry.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/iterations/iteration-001-retry.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Iteration 1 (Retry): Census Re-Verification + Artifact Conformance Repair\n2: \n3: ## Focus\n4: Retry of iteration 1 under the YAML-authorized bounded redispatch. Scope: re-verify the load-bearing evidence in the immutable `iteration-001.md` (full on-disk census of the 44 child phase folders and the validate.sh metadata surface), then repair the mechanical artifact gap — a missing `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` and a non-canonical state record lacking `iteration`/`mode`/`target_agent`/`agent_definition_loaded`/`resolved_route`. No broadening of scope; prior narrative and prior state row are preserved untouched.\n5: \n6: ## Actions Taken\n7: 1. Read `.opencode/agents/deep-research.md` (agent contract), prior `iteration-001.md`, `deep-research-state.jsonl`, and `deep-research-config.json` to re-anchor on the immutable evidence and the artifact contract. [SOURCE: deep-research-state.jsonl:1-7, deep-research-config.json:1-57]\n8: 2. Re-ran the on-disk census: `ls -d [0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` in the 036 parent → 45 dirs, 44 children + the 057 host; compared against `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` (44 entries). [SOURCE: bash census, specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/graph-metadata.json]\n9: 3. Re-verified the validate.sh embedded child manifest: extracted the hardcoded 40-entry list (001-033, 035, 047-052, last `052-cli-devin-executor-repair`) and recomputed its sha256. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh:216-219]\n10: 4. Checked `research/lineages/ds-a/deltas/` → empty; `iter-001.jsonl` was missing (the mechanical gap this retry repairs). [SOURCE: bash ls research/lineages/ds-a/deltas]\n11: 5. Appended one corrected canonical `type:iteration` record with `iteration:1`, `run:1` to the state log, and wrote the missing `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` delta stream. [SOURCE: this iteration's writes]\n12: \n13: ## Findings\n14: 1. **On-disk census confirmed:** exactly 44 child folders match `^[0-9]{3}-` (001-033, 035, 047-056) plus the 057 host = 45 dirs total. `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` holds exactly 44 entries that match the on-disk set exactly — no orphans, no stale IDs. [SOURCE: bash census + graph-metadata.json]\n15: 2. **validate.sh embedded manifest confirmed (40 of 44):** the hardcoded list at validate.sh:216-219 contains 40 entries (001-033, 035, 047-052); recomputed sha256 `f6cf1e943d39629118c976ac71b5141bb8b85198c47641815b505adf50e732e6` matches the embedded `expected_hash` exactly. Children 053-056 are absent from the embedded list. [SOURCE: validate.sh:216-219, python sha256 recompute]\n16: 3. **Mechanical gap identified and repaired:** `deltas/` contained no `iter-001.jsonl`, and the prior run-1 state row lacked the canonical `iteration`/`mode`/`target_agent`/`agent_definition_loaded`/`resolved_route` fields required by the output contract. This retry appends a corrected canonical record and writes the missing delta. [SOURCE: bash ls deltas/, deep-research-state.jsonl:2]\n17: 4. **Prior-evidence claims retained (not re-verified this pass):** the leaf (25/31) vs phase-parent (13) split, parent spec.md phase documentation map at spec.md:213-258, `manifest/phase-tree.json`, `specs/descriptions.json`, git first-add chronology, the 033-dispositions ambiguity, and the 98-file cross-repo blast radius were established in the immutable iteration-001.md and are cited as prior evidence, not re-derived here. [SOURCE: iteration-001.md:8-33]\n18: 5. **No scope violations encountered:** all reads targeted the 036 parent and spec-kit scripts; all writes stayed inside the three allowed packet-local paths. [SOURCE: this iteration's write log]\n19: \n20: ## Questions Answered\n21: None new — this retry re-confirms the census portion of KQ1's grounding and repairs artifacts; it does not answer KQ1-KQ4 (those are recorded in the prior lineage rows).\n22: \n23: ## Questions Remaining\n24: - KQ1-KQ4 remain as recorded in the prior state rows: feasibility of grouping (KQ1), cluster mapping (KQ2), migration plan (KQ3), timeline.md design (KQ4).\n25: - Open from re-verification: the validate.sh embedded manifest covers only 40/44 children (053-056 missing) — any migration must reconcile this surface (see iteration-001.md:21).\n26: \n27: ## Next Focus\n28: No new research direction. The reducer's synthesis (already emitted at deep-research-state.jsonl:7) is the completion path; any follow-up belongs to the follow-up implementation packet, not additional deep-research iterations.\n29: \n30: ## Assessment\n31: - New information ratio: 0.25 (confirmation-dominant; 1 of 4 re-verified surfaces yielded a structural observation — the missing delta artifact)\n32: - Questions addressed: none beyond census confirmation\n33: - Edge cases: partial-success — prior runs produced valid narrative + state rows but skipped the delta contract; corrected in this retry\n34: \n35: ## Reflection\n36: - What worked: independent re-derivation of the census via fresh bash + python rather than trusting prior output; recomputing the sha256 from the extracted manifest text (after unescaping the bash `$'...\\n'` literal, which initially mis-split and yielded a wrong hash on the first attempt).\n37: - What did not work: a naive regex split on the `$'...'` literal treated `\\n` as literal characters (entries=1); the corrected split on the escaped `\\n` produced the matching hash. Lesson recorded for future manifest verification.\n38: - What I would do differently: verify the byte serialization format of embedded manifests before hashing; the bash single-quoted `$'...'` string needs unescaping before sha256, which is exactly the fragile spot a migration would touch.\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 1 (Retry): Census Re-Verification + Artifact Conformance Repair\n\n## Focus\nRetry of iteration 1 under the YAML-authorized bounded redispatch. Scope: re-verify the load-bearing evidence in the immutable `iteration-001.md` (full on-disk census of the 44 child phase folders and the validate.sh metadata surface), then repair the mechanical artifact gap — a missing `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` and a non-canonical state record lacking `iteration`/`mode`/`target_agent`/`agent_definition_loaded`/`resolved_route`. No broadening of scope; prior narrative and prior state row are preserved untouched.\n\n## Actions Taken\n1. Read `.opencode/agents/deep-research.md` (agent contract), prior `iteration-001.md`, `deep-research-state.jsonl`, and `deep-research-config.json` to re-anchor on the immutable evidence and the artifact contract. [SOURCE: deep-research-state.jsonl:1-7, deep-research-config.json:1-57]\n2. Re-ran the on-disk census: `ls -d [0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` in the 036 parent → 45 dirs, 44 children + the 057 host; compared against `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` (44 entries). [SOURCE: bash census, specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/graph-metadata.json]\n3. Re-verified the validate.sh embedded child manifest: extracted the hardcoded 40-entry list (001-033, 035, 047-052, last `052-cli-devin-executor-repair`) and recomputed its sha256. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh:216-219]\n4. Checked `research/lineages/ds-a/deltas/` → empty; `iter-001.jsonl` was missing (the mechanical gap this retry repairs). [SOURCE: bash ls research/lineages/ds-a/deltas]\n5. Appended one corrected canonical `type:iteration` record with `iteration:1`, `run:1` to the state log, and wrote the missing `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` delta stream. [SOURCE: this iteration's writes]\n\n## Findings\n1. **On-disk census confirmed:** exactly 44 child folders match `^[0-9]{3}-` (001-033, 035, 047-056) plus the 057 host = 45 dirs total. `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` holds exactly 44 entries that match the on-disk set exactly — no orphans, no stale IDs. [SOURCE: bash census + graph-metadata.json]\n2. **validate.sh embedded manifest confirmed (40 of 44):** the hardcoded list at validate.sh:216-219 contains 40 entries (001-033, 035, 047-052); recomputed sha256 `f6cf1e943d39629118c976ac71b5141bb8b85198c47641815b505adf50e732e6` matches the embedded `expected_hash` exactly. Children 053-056 are absent from the embedded list. [SOURCE: validate.sh:216-219, python sha256 recompute]\n3. **Mechanical gap identified and repaired:** `deltas/` contained no `iter-001.jsonl`, and the prior run-1 state row lacked the canonical `iteration`/`mode`/`target_agent`/`agent_definition_loaded`/`resolved_route` fields required by the output contract. This retry appends a corrected canonical record and writes the missing delta. [SOURCE: bash ls deltas/, deep-research-state.jsonl:2]\n4. **Prior-evidence claims retained (not re-verified this pass):** the leaf (25/31) vs phase-parent (13) split, parent spec.md phase documentation map at spec.md:213-258, `manifest/phase-tree.json`, `specs/descriptions.json`, git first-add chronology, the 033-dispositions ambiguity, and the 98-file cross-repo blast radius were established in the immutable iteration-001.md and are cited as prior evidence, not re-derived here. [SOURCE: iteration-001.md:8-33]\n5. **No scope violations encountered:** all reads targeted the 036 parent and spec-kit scripts; all writes stayed inside the three allowed packet-local paths. [SOURCE: this iteration's write log]\n\n## Questions Answered","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/iterations/iteration-001-retry.md","text":"# Iteration 1 (Retry): Census Re-Verification + Artifact Conformance Repair\n\n## Focus\nRetry of iteration 1 under the YAML-authorized bounded redispatch. Scope: re-verify the load-bearing evidence in the immutable `iteration-001.md` (full on-disk census of the 44 child phase folders and the validate.sh metadata surface), then repair the mechanical artifact gap — a missing `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` and a non-canonical state record lacking `iteration`/`mode`/`target_agent`/`agent_definition_loaded`/`resolved_route`. No broadening of scope; prior narrative and prior state row are preserved untouched.\n\n## Actions Taken\n1. Read `.opencode/agents/deep-research.md` (agent contract), prior `iteration-001.md`, `deep-research-state.jsonl`, and `deep-research-config.json` to re-anchor on the immutable evidence and the artifact contract. [SOURCE: deep-research-state.jsonl:1-7, deep-research-config.json:1-57]\n2. Re-ran the on-disk census: `ls -d [0-9][0-9][0-9]-*/` in the 036 parent → 45 dirs, 44 children + the 057 host; compared against `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` (44 entries). [SOURCE: bash census, specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/graph-metadata.json]\n3. Re-verified the validate.sh embedded child manifest: extracted the hardcoded 40-entry list (001-033, 035, 047-052, last `052-cli-devin-executor-repair`) and recomputed its sha256. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/spec/validate.sh:216-219]\n4. Checked `research/lineages/ds-a/deltas/` → empty; `iter-001.jsonl` was missing (the mechanical gap this retry repairs). [SOURCE: bash ls research/lineages/ds-a/deltas]\n5. Appended one corrected canonical `type:iteration` record with `iteration:1`, `run:1` to the state log, and wrote the missing `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` delta stream. [SOURCE: this iteration's writes]\n\n## Findings\n1. **On-disk census confirmed:** exactly 44 child folders match `^[0-9]{3}-` (001-033, 035, 047-056) plus the 057 host = 45 dirs total. `graph-metadata.json` `children_ids` holds exactly 44 entries that match the on-disk set exactly — no orphans, no stale IDs. [SOURCE: bash census + graph-metadata.json]\n2. **validate.sh embedded manifest confirmed (40 of 44):** the hardcoded list at validate.sh:216-219 contains 40 entries (001-033, 035, 047-052); recomputed sha256 `f6cf1e943d39629118c976ac71b5141bb8b85198c47641815b505adf50e732e6` matches the embedded `expected_hash` exactly. Children 053-056 are absent from the embedded list. [SOURCE: validate.sh:216-219, python sha256 recompute]\n3. **Mechanical gap identified and repaired:** `deltas/` contained no `iter-001.jsonl`, and the prior run-1 state row lacked the canonical `iteration`/`mode`/`target_agent`/`agent_definition_loaded`/`resolved_route` fields required by the output contract. This retry appends a corrected canonical record and writes the missing delta. [SOURCE: bash ls deltas/, deep-research-state.jsonl:2]\n4. **Prior-evidence claims retained (not re-verified this pass):** the leaf (25/31) vs phase-parent (13) split, parent spec.md phase documentation map at spec.md:213-258, `manifest/phase-tree.json`, `specs/descriptions.json`, git first-add chronology, the 033-dispositions ambiguity, and the 98-file cross-repo blast radius were established in the immutable iteration-001.md and are cited as prior evidence, not re-derived here. [SOURCE: iteration-001.md:8-33]\n5. **No scope violations encountered:** all reads targeted the 036 parent and spec-kit scripts; all writes stayed inside the three allowed packet-local paths. [SOURCE: this iteration's write log]\n\n## Questions Answered\nNone new — this retry re-confirms the census portion of KQ1's grounding and repairs artifacts; it does not answer KQ1-KQ4 (those are recorded in the prior lineage rows).\n\n## Questions Remaining\n- KQ1-KQ4 remain as recorded in the prior state rows: feasibility of grouping (KQ1), cluster mapping (KQ2), migration plan (KQ3), timeline.md design (KQ4).\n- Open from re-verification: the validate.sh embedded manifest covers only 40/44 children (053-056 missing) — any migration must reconcile this surface (see iteration-001.md:21).\n\n## Next Focus\nNo new research direction. The reducer's synthesis (already emitted at deep-research-state.jsonl:7) is the completion path; any follow-up belongs to the follow-up implementation packet, not additional deep-research iterations.\n\n## Assessment\n- New information ratio: 0.25 (confirmation-dominant; 1 of 4 re-verified surfaces yielded a structural observation — the missing delta artifact)\n- Questions addressed: none beyond census confirmation\n- Edge cases: partial-success — prior runs produced valid narrative + state rows but skipped the delta contract; corrected in this retry\n\n## Reflection\n- What worked: independent re-derivation of the census via fresh bash + python rather than trusting prior output; recomputing the sha256 from the extracted manifest text (after unescaping the bash `$'...\\n'` literal, which initially mis-split and yielded a wrong hash on the first attempt).\n- What did not work: a naive regex split on the `$'...'` literal treated `\\n` as literal characters (entries=1); the corrected split on the escaped `\\n` produced the matching hash. Lesson recorded for future manifest verification.\n- What I would do differently: verify the byte serialization format of embedded manifests before hashing; the bash single-quoted `$'...'` string needs unescaping before sha256, which is exactly the fragile spot a migration would touch.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":38,"totalLines":38,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/057-phase-consolidation-research/research/lineages/ds-a/iterations/iteration-001-retry.md","time":{"start":1786606250098,"end":1786606250105}},"id":"prt_ffa07e66000173jhnlmp49O9QU","sessionID":"ses_005f8753cffeGq3BHa2N564TRT","messageID":"msg_ffa07d718001tsyYqE2mcuP6xq"}}
