{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786606299937,"sessionID":"ses_005f8753cffeGq3BHa2N564TRT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_hjpXFeOxiWXDhkm35CPS5599","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, json, re\nroot = \"specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation\"\ncands = [\"004\",\"006\",\"007\",\"008\",\"009\",\"010\",\"011\",\"012\",\"013\",\"014\",\"047\",\"048\",\"049\"]\nprint(\"=== 1. Candidate phase-parents: do they have sub-children matching ^[0-9]{3}- ? ===\")\nfor c in cands:\n    p = os.path.join(root, c)\n    sub = []\n    if os.path.isdir(p):\n        for e in sorted(os.listdir(p)):\n            if re.match(r'^\\d{3}-', e) and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(p, e)):\n                sub.append(e)\n    print(f\"{c}: parent_dir={os.path.isdir(p)} sub_children={len(sub)} first_3={sub[:3]}\")\nprint()\nprint(\"=== 2. spec.md ordering invariants (lines 148-165) ===\")\nspec = os.path.join(root, \"spec.md\")\nif os.path.isfile(spec):\n    with open(spec) as f:\n        lines = f.readlines()\n    for i in range(147, min(165, len(lines))):\n        print(f\"{i+1}: {lines[i].rstrip()}\")\nprint()\nprint(\"=== 3. manifest/phase-tree.json: declared children vs phases array ===\")\npt = os.path.join(root, \"manifest\", \"phase-tree.json\")\nif os.path.isfile(pt):\n    data = json.load(open(pt))\n    phases = data.get(\"phases\", [])\n    print(f\"live_direct_children={data.get('live_direct_children')} phases_len={len(phases)} phases_ids={[p.get('id') for p in phases][:20]}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"phase-tree.json NOT FOUND at manifest/\")\nPY","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0144-system-deep-loop-036-p0-remediation"},"output":"=== 1. Candidate phase-parents: do they have sub-children matching ^[0-9]{3}- ? ===\n004: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n006: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n007: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n008: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n009: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n010: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n011: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n012: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n013: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n014: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n047: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n048: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n049: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n\n=== 2. spec.md ordering invariants (lines 148-165) ===\n148: | **017** | `017-integrate-latest-and-closeout` | leaf | Integrate the latest origin in a clean worktree; re-census touched contracts and **reopen affected phases on relevant drift**; rerun the entire 016 gate on the exact final SHA; reconcile the 065 \"open\" items (append-only), changelogs, and packet metadata; parent rollup + merge. |\n149: \n150: **Sequencing invariants** (SOL ultra review, folded in):\n151: 1. Baseline, taxonomy, the state corpus, and the frozen 178-row rec set are frozen (003-004) before any architecture or implementation work.\n152: 2. The transition-authority + event-compatibility contract is frozen (004) before any typed event writer lands, and the authorization gateway co-lands with the first writer (006).\n153: 3. The new substrate stays **additive, dark, and non-authoritative** until legacy adapters, shadow parity, and rollback pass (008).\n154: 4. Stable logical identities + durable fan-in (009) precede novelty/claim projections (010); both precede convergence activation (011).\n155: 5. Shared mode contracts + cross-mode closures (012) land before the per-mode fan-out (013).\n156: 6. deep-improvement common services precede the agent-improvement, model-benchmark, and skill-benchmark migrations.\n157: 7. Per-mode gates prove **shadow parity only**; authority changes solely in the cutover phase (014).\n158: 8. Legacy live writers are removed (015) only after state classification, rollback rehearsal, mixed-version replay, and cutover certificates.\n159: 9. Every implementation phase strict-validates independently and produces a blocking SOL receipt bound to its exact commit.\n160: 10. The whole-system gate (016) runs on a frozen SHA and reruns after integrate-latest (017), reopening earlier phases on relevant drift.\n161: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n162: \n163: <!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n164: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n165: \n\n=== 3. manifest/phase-tree.json: declared children vs phases array ===\nlive_direct_children=44 phases_len=17 phases_ids=[None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None]\n","metadata":{"output":"=== 1. Candidate phase-parents: do they have sub-children matching ^[0-9]{3}- ? ===\n004: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n006: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n007: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n008: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n009: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n010: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n011: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n012: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n013: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n014: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n047: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n048: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n049: parent_dir=False sub_children=0 first_3=[]\n\n=== 2. spec.md ordering invariants (lines 148-165) ===\n148: | **017** | `017-integrate-latest-and-closeout` | leaf | Integrate the latest origin in a clean worktree; re-census touched contracts and **reopen affected phases on relevant drift**; rerun the entire 016 gate on the exact final SHA; reconcile the 065 \"open\" items (append-only), changelogs, and packet metadata; parent rollup + merge. |\n149: \n150: **Sequencing invariants** (SOL ultra review, folded in):\n151: 1. Baseline, taxonomy, the state corpus, and the frozen 178-row rec set are frozen (003-004) before any architecture or implementation work.\n152: 2. The transition-authority + event-compatibility contract is frozen (004) before any typed event writer lands, and the authorization gateway co-lands with the first writer (006).\n153: 3. The new substrate stays **additive, dark, and non-authoritative** until legacy adapters, shadow parity, and rollback pass (008).\n154: 4. Stable logical identities + durable fan-in (009) precede novelty/claim projections (010); both precede convergence activation (011).\n155: 5. Shared mode contracts + cross-mode closures (012) land before the per-mode fan-out (013).\n156: 6. deep-improvement common services precede the agent-improvement, model-benchmark, and skill-benchmark migrations.\n157: 7. Per-mode gates prove **shadow parity only**; authority changes solely in the cutover phase (014).\n158: 8. Legacy live writers are removed (015) only after state classification, rollback rehearsal, mixed-version replay, and cutover certificates.\n159: 9. Every implementation phase strict-validates independently and produces a blocking SOL receipt bound to its exact commit.\n160: 10. The whole-system gate (016) runs on a frozen SHA and reruns after integrate-latest (017), reopening earlier phases on relevant drift.\n161: <!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n162: \n163: <!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n164: ## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n165: \n\n=== 3. manifest/phase-tree.json: declared children vs phases array ===\nlive_direct_children=44 phases_len=17 phases_ids=[None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None, None]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, json, re\nroot = \"specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation\"\ncands = [\"004\",\"006\",\"007\",\"008\",\"009\",\"010\",\"011\",\"012\",\"013\",\"014\",\"047\",\"048\",\"049\"]\nprint(\"=== 1. Candidate phase-parents: do they have sub-children matching ^[0-9]{3}- ? ===\")\nfor c in cands:\n    p = os.path.join(root, c)\n    sub = []\n    if os.path.isdir(p):\n        for e in sorted(os.listdir(p)):\n            if re.match(r'^\\d{3}-', e) and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(p, e)):\n                sub.append(e)\n    print(f\"{c}: parent_dir={os.path.isdir(p)} sub_children={len(sub)} first_3={sub[:3]}\")\nprint()\nprint(\"=== 2. spec.md ordering invariants (lines 148-165) ===\")\nspec = os.path.join(root, \"spec.md\")\nif os.path.isfile(spec):\n    with open(spec) as f:\n        lines = f.readlines()\n    for i in range(147, min(165, len(lines))):\n        print(f\"{i+1}: {lines[i].rstrip()}\")\nprint()\nprint(\"=== 3. manifest/phase-tree.json: declared children vs phases array ===\")\npt = os.path.join(root, \"manifest\", \"phase-tree.json\")\nif os.path.isfile(pt):\n    data = json.load(open(pt))\n    phases = data.get(\"phases\", [])\n    print(f\"live_direct_children={data.get('live_direct_children')} phases_len={len(phases)} phases_ids={[p.get('id') for p in phases][:20]}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"phase-tree.json NOT FOUND at manifest/\")\nPY","time":{"start":1786606299932,"end":1786606299936}},"id":"prt_ffa08a0d3001mEQNAKR1t85prp","sessionID":"ses_005f8753cffeGq3BHa2N564TRT","messageID":"msg_ffa07edd6001T9txYEDsv6d2wl"}}
